# React Native Starter Kit Development Guidelines
- Use functional programming approach instead of class-based
- All services should export both named functions and a default combined export
- Use TypeScript for all files with proper types and interfaces
- Use NativeWind (Tailwind CSS) for styling components
- Never hardcode strings, always use i18n.t() for translations
- Wrap service functions in try-catch blocks with proper error handling
- Keep UI components pure when possible
- Use react-hook-form with yup for form handling
- Follow the folder structure pattern:
  - app/(app) - Main app screens
  - app/(auth) - Authentication screens
  - components - Reusable UI components
  - context - React context providers
  - services - Core business logic and services
  - hooks - Custom React hooks
  - translations - Language files
  - types - TypeScript types 